    "q-71572": {
      "dom_id": "step-q71572",
      "name": "Question 4",
      "problem": "For the function $f(x,y,z)={x}^{2}-{y}^{2}+z-2,$ find the equation of the level surface $f(x,y,z)=-2.$",
      "worked_solution": "Recall that the level surfaces for the function $f(x,y,z)$ are given by the equation\n\n$$\nf(x,y,z)=c.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we're interested in $c=-2.$ So, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y,z) & =c \\\\ {x}^{2}-{y}^{2}+z-2 & =-2 \\\\ z & ={y}^{2}-{x}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the level surface for $c=-2$ is the hyperbolic paraboloid $z={y}^{2}-{x}^{2}.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
