    "q-71590": {
      "dom_id": "step-q71590",
      "name": "Question 8",
      "problem": "Which of the following describes the level surfaces of the function $f(x,y,z)=\\frac{\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡z}{x+y}?$",
      "worked_solution": "The level surfaces of the function $f(x,y,z)$ are given by the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y,z) & =c \\\\ \\frac{\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡z}{x+y} & =c \\\\ \\operatorname{arcsin}⁡z & =c(x+y) \\\\ z & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(c(x+y))\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we get a family of surfaces given by:\n\n$$\nz=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(c(x+y)),\\,c\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-71590-a",
              "type": "text",
              "value": "A family of surfaces given by $z=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(c(x+y))$",
