    "q-129199": {
      "dom_id": "step-q129199",
      "name": "Question 9",
      "problem": "Which of the following describes the level surfaces of the function $f(x,y,z)={e}^{4{x}^{2}+9{y}^{2}-z-3}?$",
      "worked_solution": "The level surfaces of the function $f(x,y,z)$ are given by the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y,z) & =c \\\\ {e}^{4{x}^{2}+9{y}^{2}-z-3} & =c \\\\ 4{x}^{2}+9{y}^{2}-z-3 & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡c \\\\ z & =4{x}^{2}+9{y}^{2}-3-\\operatorname{ln}⁡c,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $c>0.$\n\nTherefore, we get a family of elliptic paraboloids:\n\n$$\nz=4{x}^{2}+9{y}^{2}-3-\\operatorname{ln}⁡c,\\,c\\in (0,\\infty )\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
